      "title": "Top K Frequent Elements",
      "type": "LEETCODE",
      "notesMarkdown": "- used new Array({length: n}).fill([]) method to add the empty array to the bucket - problem is it creates reference to the same slot. instead use Array.from({}, () => [])\n- Object.entries to get the count and value over Map wont work - instead use the forEach method -The Fix: Use elMap.forEach((count, num) => ...) or a for...of loop like for (let [num, count] of elMap).\n\n- result.slice(k)The Problem: .slice(k) extracts elements starting from index k to the end. If $k=2$ and your result is [1, 2], slice(2) gives you an empty array.The Fix: You want the first $k$ elements, so use .slice(0, k)",
